.TH FKSTRCAT 3 2026-09-24 "fkstring" "fkstring Library Manual"
.nh
.SH NAME
fkstrcat, fkstrcatc, fkstrcatone \- append to an fkstring
.SH LIBRARY
fkstring library
.RI ( libfkstring ,\~ \-lfkstring )
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <fkstring.h>
.PP
.BI "fkstring *fkstrcat(fkstring *" dst ", const fkstring *" src );
.BI "fkstring *fkstrcatc(fkstring *" dst ", const char *" src );
.BI "fkstring *fkstrcatone(fkstring *" dst ", char " c );
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
These functions append to
.I dst
in place.
.BR fkstrcat ()
appends the
.B fkstring
.IR src ,
including any embedded NUL bytes.
.BR fkstrcatc ()
appends the NUL-terminated string
.IR src ;
a NULL or empty
.I src
leaves
.I dst
unchanged.
.BR fkstrcatone ()
appends the single byte
.IR c ,
which may be
.BR \(aq\e0\(aq .
.PP
When
.I dst
has no room left, its buffer grows by the bump factor described in
.BR fkstring (3),
so a sequence of appends reallocates only occasionally.
.PP
.I src
may be
.I dst
itself, or point into
.IR dst 's
buffer:
.I fkstrcat(s,\~s)
doubles
.IR s .
.SH RETURN VALUE
.IR dst ,
or NULL, leaving
.I dst
unchanged, if
.I dst
is NULL, or if the
.I src
of
.BR fkstrcat ()
is.
.SH ERRORS
These functions do not return on allocation failure; see
.BR fkstring (3).
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
fkstring *s = fkstrnew("foo");
\&
fkstrcatc(s, "bar");      /* "foobar" */
fkstrcatone(s, \(aq!\(aq);     /* "foobar!" */
fkstrcat(s, s);           /* "foobar!foobar!" */
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fkstring (3),
.BR fkinsert (3),
.BR fksprintf (3),
.BR fkjoin (3)
